column20:
I'm really exited about the new concurrency libraries, things like Parallel LINQ and the Task Parallel Library.<p>To think that you can write code such as:<p><pre><code>  void Render(Scene scene, Color[,] rgb)
  {  
    Parallel.For(0, screenHeight, y => 
    {
      for (int x = 0; x < screenWidth; x++) {
        rgb[x,y] = TraceRay(new Ray(scene,x,y));
      }
    });
  }
</code></pre>
and<p><pre><code>    var q = src.AsParallel()
        .Where(x => ExpensiveFilter(x));
    foreach(var x in q) { ... }

</code></pre>
just has to make you grin from ear to ear.
